>> title: Toum
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: garlic, lebanese, emulsion, dip, food processor
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: thoum, toom, garlic sauce, garlic paste, Lebanese garlic sauce
>> pairs-with: pita-bread
>> servings: 12
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the oil goes in hair-thin with the machine running, and a toum that breaks is a bowl of garlic oil rather than a white cream; it is rescued by starting again with a fresh spoonful and adding the broken batch back, not by pulsing harder
>> step.1: pulse to a fine paste
>> step.2: pulse in
>> step.3: stream in hair-thin, machine running
>> step.4: pulse in to set the emulsion

Pulse @garlic{1/2%cup}(70 g; peeled cloves) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} to a fine paste in a #food processor{}, scraping the bowl down twice.

Pulse @lemon juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)garlic paste{} in three additions.

Stream @neutral oil{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL) into @&(~1)garlic{} in a hair-thin thread with the machine running, taking a full ~{8%min}.

Pulse @ice water{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)toum{} until it turns white and fluffy.
